Negative control for the BOOT-AS-SELF law (`R6-30b`).

Boots an unqualified page at CLIENT instead of SELF — the declaration-supplied
actor the contract deleted, put back as a hardcoded default. Nothing else
moves: a url carrying `/as/:actor` still wins, so what this withdraws is only
the law that a page with NO actor segment is the acting user.

Re-pointed for `R7-14`: the default moved off the `.as()` call and onto the
`actor` the matrix gate is asked about first, so the control mutates the ONE
place the boot actor is decided rather than the call site's former copy of it.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the port spec — a boot with no scope override resolves the SELF actor.

